      "sha256": "49bc036d9ac2d9aef65e628302c173038deb6a737697ce0086256491c422c9a1",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Figure 7. Sixteen participants rate usefulness, ease of use, and ease of learning for nine SPARK features: progress visualization, element inspector, element previewer, simulated interactions, real-time code boxes, timestamp code boxes, AI-generated tests, checkpoint verification, and the reference panel. Agree and strongly agree dominate every bar. All sixteen strongly agree that checkpoint verification is easy to use and easy to learn. Fifteen strongly agree that AI-generated tests are easy to use and learn. The few other responses are neutral, disagree, or not used; no strongly-disagree segment is visible."
